── UNKNOWN NAME ───────── E0211_null_where_an_option_is_written.lt:2:28  [E0211]

Stilt has no `null`: a missing value is `None`:

  2 │   var found: Option<i64> = null
    │                            ^^^^

A value that may be missing has the type `Option<T>`: it is `None` when the
value is missing and `Some(x)` when it is there, and a `match` or an `else`
reads it.

To fix it, write `None`:

  2 │   var found: Option<i64> = None
    │                            ~~~~
